**CONTRACT EXCERPT FOR MANUFACTURING AND QUALITY CONTROL SERVICES** **This Manufacturing and Quality Control Services Agreement (hereinafter referred to as the “Agreement”) is made on this 15th day of March, 2023, by and between:** **1. ACME Manufacturing Solutions LLC** A limited liability company incorporated under the laws of the State of New Jersey, having its principal place of business at 123 Industrial Park Drive, Newark, NJ 07102 (hereinafter referred to as “ACME”). **2. BetaTech Industries Inc.** A corporation incorporated under the laws of the State of California, having its principal place of business at 456 Tech Lane, San Jose, CA 95112 (hereniafter referred to as “BetaTech”). **RECITALS** WHEREAS, ACME is engaged in the business of manufacturing industrial equipment and machinery, with a specialization in automation systems; WHEREAS, BetaTech is engaged in the design and assembly of electronic components and has expertise in quality control processes for various industrial applications; WHEREAS, ACME desires to engage BetaTech for the provision of manufacturing services and quality control oversight of its production lines for the upcoming fiscal year 2023-2024; WHEREAS, BetaTech agrees to provide such services under the terms and conditions set forth in this Agreement. **NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the parties agree as follows:** **1. DEFINITIONS** 1.1 "Facilities" refers to the manufacturing plants operated by ACME located at 123 Industrial Park Drive, Newark, NJ, and its secondary facility at 789 Production Road, Philadelphia, PA 19101. 1.2 "Production Lines" refers to the assembly lines operated by ACME within the Facilities, specifically Line A (Automated Assembly), Line B (Component Fabrication), and Line C (Quality Assurance). 1.3 "Quality Control Procedures" refers to the systematic processes established to ensure that the production output meets the specifications set forth in Exhibit A. 1.4 "Personnel" refers to the employees, contractors, and any ohter representatives of both ACME and BetaTech who are involved in the execution of this Agreement. **2. SCOPE OF SERVICES** 2.1 ACME hereby engages BetaTech to provide the following services (collectively referred to as the “Services”): a. Oversight of the Quality Control Procedures on all Production Lines, ensuring compliance with industry standards and regulatory requirements. b. Routine inspections and assessments of equipment, including but not limited to the Automated Guided Vehicles (AGVs) and CNC machines, to maintain operational efficiency. c. Training Programs for ACME Personnel on the proper operation of industrial equipment and adherence to quality standards. d. Documentation and reporting of quality metrics and discrepancies to ACME’s Quality Assurance Manager, Mr. John Smith, at least bi-weekly. **3. TERM AND TERMINATION** 3.1 This Agreement shall commence on April 1, 2023, and shall continue in full force and effect until March 31, 2024, unless terminated earlier by either party in accordance with Section 3.2. 3.2 Either party may terminate this Agreement for cause if the other party fails to perform any material obligation under this Agreement and does not cure such failure within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice from the non-defaulting party. **4. COMPENSATION** 4.1 In consideration of the Services rendered by BetaTech, ACME agrees to pay BetaTech a fee of $300,000 for the term of this Agreement, payable in four quarterly installments of $75,000 each, due on the first day of each quarter. 4.2 Additional services requested by ACME beyond the scope outlined in Section 2 shall be billed at the rate of $150 per hour, with prior written approval from ACME. **5. RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE PARTIES** 5.1 ACME shall: a. Provide BetaTech with access to the Facilities during regular business hours for the purpose of conducting inspections and oversight. b. Ensure that all Personnel involved in the production process are adequately trained and informed regarding the Quality Control Procedures. c. Provide all necessary data and reports pertaining to production output and previous quality assessments to facilitate BetaTech’s oversight. 5.2 BetaTech shall: a. Assign a dedicated Quality Control Supervisor, Ms. Laura Johnson, to oversee the implementation and adherence to Quality Control Procedures. b. Provide a monthly report to ACME’s management team, including the Operations Manager, Mr. James Lee, detailing findings, recommendations, and actionable insights to improve production quality. c. Ensure that all Personnel are adequately trained in quality control measures and the operation of industrial equipment. **6. CONFIDENTIALITY** 6.1 Each party agrees to maintain the confidentiality of all proprietary information disclosed during the term of this Agreement, including, but not limited to, production methods, quality control processes, and business strategies. 6.2 Confidentiality obligations shall survive the termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years. **7. INDEMNIFICATION** 7.1 BetaTech agrees to indemnify and hold harmless ACME, its officers, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, or liabilities arising from BetaTech’s negligence or willful misconduct in the performance of the Services. 7.2 ACME agrees to indemnify and hold harmless BetaTech, its officers, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, or liabilities arising from ACME’s negligence or willful misconduct in connection with this Agreement. **8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY** 8.1 Neither party shall be liable to the other for any indirect, special, or consequential damages arising out of this Agreement, whether based on breach of contract, tort (including negligence), or any other legal theory. **9. DISPUTE RESOLUTION** 9.1 Any disputes arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall be resolved through binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association. The arbitration shall take place in Newark, New Jersey. **10. MISCELLANEOUS** 10.1 This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior negotiations, representations, and agreements, whether written or oral. 10.2 This Agreement may not be amended or modified except in writing signed by both parties. 10.3 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New Jersey. 10.4 If any provision of this Agreement is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect. **IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties hereto have executed this Manufacturing and Quality Control Services Agreement as of the date first above written. **ACME Manufacturing Solutions LLC** By: ___________________________ Name: Mr. Richard Adams Title: Chief Executive Officer Date: __________________________ **BetaTech Industries Inc.** By: ___________________________ Name: Ms. Sarah Thompson Title: Chief Operating Officer Date: __________________________ **EXHIBIT A** **Quality Control Specifications:** 1. **Inspection Standards** - All components must meet the specifications outlined in the ISO 9001:2015 certification standards. 2. **Testing Equipment** - Utilize calibrated testing equipment such as the Mitutoyo Coordinate Measuring Machine (CMM) Model CRYSTA-Apex S for dimensional verification. 3. **Documentation** - All inspections must be documented and retained for a minimum of five years for compliance purposes. 4. **Performance Metrics** - Acceptable defect rate muts not exceed 2% per production batch. 5. **Training Requirements** - All Personnel involved in the quality control process must complete the ACME Quality Assurance Training Program prior to commencing work on the Production Lines. **END OF DOCUMENT**